## Conventions (every change)

- Strict types. No escape hatches without a comment justifying each one.
- Pure domain logic is side-effect-free and lives apart from IO, so the core is
  testable without infrastructure.
- Integer math for balances — never floats.
- Mutating operations follow this exact shape:
  `authenticate → validate → rate-limit → begin tx → lock row → re-validate →
  mutate → audit-log → commit`.
- Every mutating action writes an audit row inside the same transaction.
- Anything random uses a **stored seed** so outcomes are reproducible.
- **Migrations are additive-only** (rollback is redeploying the previous
  image, not down-migrations). A hand-written migration must also be
  registered wherever the migration runner looks — an unregistered migration
  silently never runs.

## Definition of done (a feature is not done without all of these)

- Validated at the boundary, transactional, rate-limited where exposed,
  audit-logged.
- Pure logic unit-tested: happy path **plus at least one exploit/edge case**.
- Tunable values pulled from config, not hardcoded.
- Reflected in the client read-only first, then wired to the action.
- The full local gate passes before the work is declared finished:
  `{{VERIFY_COMMAND}}`.

