## Local dev ports on the product owner's machine (multi-session convention)

Parallel agent sessions share one machine and one dev database.

- **Ports {{OWNER_PORTS}} are reserved for the product owner's local**,
  serving current `main`. Never take these ports, kill their processes, or
  leave them serving branch code.
- **Feature/QA sessions use alternate ports**, set in that worktree's root
  `.env`.
- **Test runs use an isolated database — dev servers stay up.** The suite runs
  against `TEST_DATABASE_URL` (root `.env`). Don't run two sessions' full
  suites simultaneously against the same test database.
- **If the reserved pair is down or serving branch code, restore it.**

Only applies on the shared local machine — CI and cloud agent VMs ignore it.

## Planning docs discipline

- All planning/design/status/spec documents live in the `planning/` directory
  (tracked in git). **Never create planning or status docs at the repo root**
  or anywhere else in the tree.
- Planning docs are product-owner input: treat them as read-mostly. Edit one
  only when explicitly asked; never move or delete anything under `planning/`
  without being asked.
- The one exception is `planning/WORK-<slug>.md`, a coding agent's own
  execution tracker for a single effort (written by the `/dev-loop` skill).
  `WORK-*` files are agent-owned; every other prefix is product-owner-owned.
- When orienting on a task, consult `planning/BUILD-SPEC.md` and
  `planning/BACKLOG.md`.
